{
  "_purpose": "The benign half of the detonation corpus, reproducibly fetchable.",
  "_why": [
    "Five benign samples cannot measure a false-positive rate, and tuning against",
    "three is what produced the regression where every signed installer came out",
    "malicious. Worse, detonation is not deterministic: the same 7-Zip binary was",
    "called malicious on one run and suspicious on a rerun the next morning,",
    "because an unrelated Windows service acted during the first one. A corpus of",
    "five measures noise.",
    "",
    "Chosen for DIVERSITY OF TOOLCHAIN, not popularity, because that is what the",
    "false positives keyed on: NSIS, Inno, WiX/MSI, SFX, MSIX, Squirrel, Go, Rust,",
    ".NET, MinGW (.bss), MSVC, plus documents and scripts. Several entries are",
    "deliberately hard - NirSoft ships UPX-packed and unsigned, PsExec is the most",
    "flagged legitimate binary in existence, rustup-init is a downloader by design,",
    "rclone is what ransomware crews use to exfiltrate, and Process Explorer reads",
    "other processes' memory as its whole function."
  ],
  "_size_cap_bytes": 33554432,
  "_size_cap_note": [
    "backend/app/config.py max_sample_mb defaults to 32 and the API answers 413",
    "above it. Nothing larger has ever been accepted by this deployment - the",
    "reason git.exe (68 MB) and vlc.exe (43 MB) are absent from the last corpus run",
    "is that they were REJECTED, not skipped. Entries over the cap are kept here,",
    "marked, and skipped by the fetcher unless the cap is raised."
  ],
  "_verification": "Every URL was probed with a ranged GET and returned 206 with the recorded size and magic on 2026-07-28. Re-run the fetcher to re-verify; sizes drift as vendors publish.",
